//! Precomputed artifacts of the F2 genus-95 product code, baked from the Sage
//! source of truth in `succinctlabs/AG_codes` (`F2_human_audit/`).
//!
//! These were parsed once from the original `.sage` files (the evaluator file
//! alone is ~1 MB) and emitted here as constants so this crate carries no Sage
//! text, no parse-time cost, and no runtime I/O.  Do not hand-edit: to refresh,
//! re-run the parser in the upstream repo and regenerate this data.
//!
//! NOTE: the base coordinates have been permuted so the 30 third-derivative
//! points are coordinates 0..29 — this makes the order-3 "restrict to points"
//! operation a low-30-bit mask, so the per-factor restrictions need not be
//! stored. R1/R2 are conjugated and R3 column-permuted accordingly, and the
//! gamma functional masks are permuted to match the reordered product
//! coordinates.
//!
//!   - `R_ROWS`: the 222 rows of the binary R matrix, each a 64-bit mask over
//!     the base-message bits.
//!   - `PRODUCT_DENOMINATOR`: the common evaluator denominator, as a degree
//!     bitmask in `x`.
//!   - `GAMMA_SLOT_MASKS`: per-slot numerator bitmasks over the 222 product
//!     coordinates (4×u64 limbs each).
//!   - `BASE_DENOMINATOR` / `BASE_GAMMA_SLOT_MASKS`: the same artifacts for the
//!     direct base-code evaluator (64 coordinates, 1×u64 limb each), in the same
//!     reordered base coordinates as the product artifacts. (Upstream now ships
//!     this ordering — the third-derivative points are 0..29 — so the σ applied
//!     when baking these was the identity; they match upstream as-is.)
//!   - `ARTIN_SCHREIER_RHS`: the right-hand-side rational coefficients used by
//!     the sampling sanity-check tests (numerator/denominator degree bitmasks).

